* {{enPR|dī-dăkˈtĭk}}, {{IPA|en|/daɪˈdæk.tɪk/|/dɪˈdæk.tɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-didactic.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-didactic.oga|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|æktɪk|s=3}}
* {{hyphenation|en|di|dac|tic}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[instructive|Instructive]] or intended to [[teach]] or [[demonstrate]], especially with regard to [[morality]].
#: {{syn|en|educative|instructive}}
#: {{ux|en|'''didactic''' poetry}}
#* {{RQ:Carlyle French Revolution|text=Falling Bastilles, Insurrections of Women, thousands of smoking Manorhouses, a country bristling with no crop but that of Sansculottic steel: these were tolerably '''didactic''' lessons; but them [the Nobility] they have not taught.}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay Goldsmith|passage=The finest '''didactic''' poem in any language.}}
# Excessively [[moralizing]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} Teaching from [[textbook]]s rather than laboratory [[demonstration]] and clinical [[application]].

